摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Structure-aware tools for AI agents. Tree-sitter code editing, web page navigation, search. No daemon, no JSON, just stdin.","id":"gh:1184970538","install_available":false,"language":"Go","name":"organon","slug":"tta-lab/organon","topics":["dsh-plugin","mcp-server","pi-extension"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Structure-aware tools for AI agents. Tree-sitter code editing, web page navigation, search. No daemo"},{"id":"p1s2","text":"n, no JSON, just stdin."},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# organon"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Structure-aware tools for AI agents, plus small workflow CLIs used in the tta-lab workspace."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Organon provides commands that give logos agents structured perception of code, running inside a tem"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"des commands that give logos agents structured perception of code, running inside a temenos sandbox."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Commands"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"### `src` — Source files"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"Read and edit code, config, and docs by symbol. Tree-sitter parses the file into an AST, assigns eac"},{"id":"p8s2","text":"h symbol a 2-char ID, and you reference symbols by ID — no text matching, no multiline quoting probl"},{"id":"p8s3","text":"mbol a 2-char ID, and you reference symbols by ID — no text matching, no multiline quoting problems."},{"id":"p9s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p10s1","text":"Supports symbol-aware extraction for Go, Rust, TypeScript, TSX, Python, C, C++, Java, Ruby, JavaScri"},{"id":"p10s2","text":"pt, and many more via auto-inference. Language is detected from file extension. Markdown uses headin"},{"id":"p10s3","text":" via auto-inference. Language is detected from file extension. Markdown uses heading-based sections."},{"id":"p11s1","text":"`src edit` is a text-based escape hatch for files where symbol editing is overkill (config files, un"},{"id":"p11s2","text":"supported languages, quick edits). It uses exact match with whitespace normalization fallbacks and w"},{"id":"p11s3","text":"orks on any text file regardless of language support."},{"id":"p12s1","text":"### `skill` — Skill discovery"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"List, find, and read agent skills from project-local and global skill directories."},{"id":"p14s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"### `nd-playlist` — Navidrome playlists as code"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"Create, update, diff, and export Navidrome playlists through the Subsonic/OpenSubsonic API."},{"id":"p17s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"Default config lives at `~/.config/nd-playlist/config.toml`:"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"`--server`, `--username`, `--password`, `NAVIDROME_URL`, `NAVIDROME_USER`, and\n`NAVIDROME_PASS` over"},{"id":"p20s2","text":"ride local config. If no password source is configured and\nstdin is a terminal, `nd-playlist` prompt"},{"id":"p20s3","text":"s for the password. Playlist YAML\nexports include song IDs but never include secrets."},{"id":"p21s1","text":"Radio YAML uses `name`, `stream_url`, and optional `homepage_url`. `radio diff`\nmatches stations by "},{"id":"p21s2","text":"stream URL and `radio apply --yes` creates only missing\nstations. Keep machine-owned station files u"},{"id":"p21s3","text":"nder `playlists/navidrome/`, which\nis ignored by Git. Navidrome requires an admin account for this g"},{"id":"p21s4","text":"ts/navidrome/`, which\nis ignored by Git. Navidrome requires an admin account for this global change."},{"id":"p22s1","text":"### `og` — guarded forge operations"},{"id":"p23s1","text":"`og issue` reads GitHub and Forgejo repository issues without depending on the\ncheckout branch:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"Writes are typed-MCP-only: `issue_create`, `issue_update_title`,\n`issue_replace_body`, `issue_edit_b"},{"id":"p25s2","text":"ody`, and `issue_comment`. Creation requires\nboth title and body (the body may be empty); title, who"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"le body, exact batch body\nedits, and comments are independent. Exact edits match each old text once "},{"id":"p25s4","text":"in\nthe body just fetched, reject duplicate/missing/ambiguous/overlapping or no-op\nedits before one b"},{"id":"p25s5","text":"ody update, and preserve all other Markdown bytes. They do\nnot provide remote compare-and-swap: a si"},{"id":"p25s6","text":"multaneous remote edit can race.\nList defaults to open, search to all; pagination defaults to page 1"},{"id":"p25s7","text":" / 30 items\nand accepts at most 100. Comments are oldest first. Provider search ranking and\ntokeniza"},{"id":"p25s8","text":"tion differ, and neither uncertain creates nor comments are retried."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"`pr_edit_body` is the typed MCP counterpart to `issue_edit_body`, using the\nsame exact `oldText`/`ne"},{"id":"p26s2","text":"wText` batch envelope:"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p28s1","text":"For an issue, call `issue_edit_body` with `issue_id` instead of `pr_id`.\nOmit `pr_id` to target the "},{"id":"p28s2","text":"current branch's PR; an explicit positive ID works\nwithout a current branch. Both tools require a no"},{"id":"p28s3","text":"nempty batch and nonempty,\nunique original-body matches; empty `newText` deletes. PR edits preserve "},{"id":"p28s4","text":"the\ntitle and comments. An uncertain write is not automatically retried; a\nprovider error after writ"},{"id":"p28s5","text":"ing does not guarantee rollback."},{"id":"p29s1","text":"`og` runs GitHub PR and Git network operations directly inside the calling CLI or MCP\nprocess. Confi"},{"id":"p29s2","text":"gure exactly one GitHub mode: an owner-scoped fine-grained PAT or\na GitHub App. `GITHUB_TOKEN`, `GH_"},{"id":"p29s3","text":"TOKEN`, and `github_token_env` are not used.\nForgejo continues to use its token environment variable"},{"id":"p29s4","text":"s. GitHub merge and CI\nqueries are unsupported in both modes; GitHub PR view omits CI. Forgejo keeps"},{"id":"p29s5","text":"\nmerge and CI status, while CI logs and failure details are outside og."},{"id":"p30s1","text":"Controlled `og` Git transport honors only a supported user-global `http.version`\nvalue (`HTTP/1.1` o"},{"id":"p30s2","text":"r `HTTP/2`); all other global and system Git configuration\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p31s1","text":"### GitHub authentication setup"},{"id":"p32s1","text":"Choose **one** section in `~/.config/ttal/og.toml`: `[github_pat]` or\n`[github_app]`. Configuring bo"},{"id":"p32s2","text":"th is an error. PAT mode uses exactly one resource\nowner, checked before reading credentials. Out-of"},{"id":"p32s3","text":"-owner Git clone and pull may\nproceed anonymously for public repositories; writes and API operations"},{"id":"p32s4","text":" are\nrejected. In-scope authentication failures never fall back to anonymous access\nor an App. App m"},{"id":"p32s5","text":"ode\nretains its allowed-owner and repository-scoped installation token behavior."},{"id":"p33s1","text":"To create a fine-grained PAT, open GitHub **Settings → Developer settings →\nPersonal access tokens →"},{"id":"p33s2","text":" Fine-grained tokens → Generate new token**. Choose a\nname and expiration, select the organization o"},{"id":"p33s3","text":"r user as **Resource owner**,\nand select only the repositories og needs. Request the repository perm"},{"id":"p33s4","text":"issions\nbelow. The token cannot exceed the creator's own repository access. An\norganization may bloc"},{"id":"p33s5","text":"k PATs, restrict expiration, or require owner approval; a\npending token can only read public resourc"},{"id":"p33s6","text":"es until approved. See GitHub's\ntoken instructions\nand organization policy."},{"id":"p34s1","text":"| Repository permission | Read-only use | Write use |"},{"id":"p35s1","text":"| Contents | Read for clone and pull | Read and write for push and tags |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p36s1","text":"## Why"},{"id":"p37s1","text":"AI agents that work via shell commands (like logos) can't do multiline file edits. Every existing ed"},{"id":"p37s2","text":"it tool uses structured JSON parameters — `{\"path\":\"file\",\"edits\":[{\"oldText\":\"...\",\"newText\":\"...\"}"},{"id":"p37s3","text":"]}` — which requires a tool-calling protocol, not shell."},{"id":"p38s1","text":"Organon solves this by replacing text matching with **symbol targeting**. The LLM doesn't need to re"},{"id":"p38s2","text":"produce the old code — it asks for the symbol tree, picks an ID, and pipes the new code via a single"},{"id":"p38s3","text":" heredoc. One stdin arg instead of two JSON fields."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
